=== front matter ===
SOCIO-DEMOGRAPHIC DATA - POPULATION 
0. Prerequisites 
0.1 Legal environment 0.1.1 Responsibility for collecting, processing, and disseminating statistics 
 
Office of Planning and Statistics 
The Statistics Act of 2011 gives the Office of Planning and Statistics (OPS) of the Ministry of Finance 
the authority to collect, compile and disseminate Palau’s statistical data. 
0.1.2 Data sharing and coordination among data producing agencies 
 
Office of Planning and Statistics 
The OPS does data sharing and coordination with a variety of agencies in Palau. Of these, the most 
important are Social Security Administration (especially on labor statistics), Financial Institutions 
Commission (on banking statistics), and Ministry of Finance (on government finance statistics). These 
data sharing and coordination arrangements work effectively. 
0.1.3 Confidentiality of individual reporters' data 
 
Office of Planning and Statistics 
Confidentiality of individual reporters’ data is protected through a number of ways. First, the Statistics 
Act of 2011 provides for protection of confidentiality (Section 204). Second, OPS staff is required 
take an oath of protecting confidentiality. Third, computer passwords also protect individual data 
confidentiality. 
0.1.4 Ensuring statistical reporting 
 
Office of Planning and Statistics 
Statistical reporting of data is ensured by the fact that the Statistics Act of 2011 gives the OPS 
authority to collect statistical data. 
 
0.2 Resources 0.2.1 Staff, facilities, computing resources, and financing 
The Office of Planning and Statistics (OPS) conducts Palau’s population censuses, and publishes its 
population statistics with the help of 10 employees—including contract employees hired for the census 
period. 
 
1. Integrity 
1.2 Transparency 1.2.1 Disclosure of terms and conditions for statistical collection, processing, and dissemination 
 
Office of Planning and Statistics 
The Statistics Act of 2011, which is available to the public, spells out the terms and conditions for the 
collection, compilation and dissemination of Palau’s statistical data. 
1.2.2 Internal governmental access to statistics prior to release 
 
Office of Planning and Statistics 
Statistical data compiled by the OPS are reviewed by the Director prior to publication. 
1.2.4 Advance notice of major changes in methodology, source data, and statistical techniques. 
 
SOCIO-DEMOGRAPHIC DATA - POPULATION 
Office of Planning and Statistics 
No advance notice given. 
 
2. Methodology 
2.1 Concepts and definitions 2.1.1 Concepts and definitions 
The concepts and definitions used for population statistics are taken from the United 
Nations, Handbook on Population and Housing Census: Concepts and Definitions. 
 
2.2 Scope Scope of the data 
All 9 inhabited islands of Palau are covered in population statistics. 
Exceptions to coverage 
No exceptions to coverage. 
 
2.3 Classification/sectorization 2.3.1 Classification/sectorization 
Census results are classified in various following ways—by gender, by island, by age group, by ethnic 
group, by religion, by marital status, by educational level, by occupational group, by economic 
activity, by employment status. 
 
3. Accuracy and reliability 
3.1 Source data 3.1.1 Source data collection programs 
Population numbers are derived from census results. The latest census was conducted on April 1, 2005 
(“the National Census Day”). Everybody present in the country on that day was counted. The census 
was conducted by about 60 field workers who visited households and institutions for counting people 
and interviewing them with a Household and Personal Questionnaire, which was designed by the US 
Census Bureau. 
 
3.5 Revision studies 3.5.1 Revision studies and analyses 
No revision studies are conducted as no revisions are done. 
 
4. Serviceability 
4.1 Periodicity and timeliness 4.1.1 Periodicity 
Population statistics are generally compiled and disseminated every 5 years. The last census was 
conducted in April 2005. Palau missed 2010 census as no budget funding was available. In December 
2012, a mini-census was conducted. 
 
4.1.2 Timeliness 
 
Population statistics derived from the April 2005 Census were disseminated in December 2005. This 
SOCIO-DEMOGRAPHIC DATA - POPULATION 
gave a timeliness of 9 months. 
 
4.3 Revision 4.3.1 Revision schedule 
 
Population size and composition. Births, deaths, and migration. 
No revision schedule has been published as no revisions are done. 
4.3.2 Identification of preliminary and/or revised data 
 
Population size and composition. Births, deaths, and migration. 
No revisions are done to published population statistics. 
 
5. Accessibility 
5.1 Data 5.1.1 Statistical presentation 
Population statistics are presented in tables accompanied by charts. 
Hard copy - Other 
Economic Statistics, Graduate School USA. 
Statistical Yearbook, Office of Planning and Statistics (OPS). 
Electronic - Other 
OPS website: www.palaugov.net/stats. 
5.1.3 Advance release calendar 
 
Office of Planning and Statistics 
No ARC published. 
5.1.4 Simultaneous release 
 
Office of Planning and Statistics 
Statistical data are simultaneously released to all, usually through the OPS’s website. 
 
5.2 Metadata 5.2.1 Dissemination of documentation on concepts, scope, classifications, basis of recording, data 
sources, and statistical techniques 
Metadata are published in the census publications available on the OPS website. 
 
9. Plans 
